{
    "question_text": "<h3>61. Rotate List</h3><p>Given the <code>head</code> of a linked list, rotate the list to the right by <code>k</code> places.</p>",
    "input_format": "The head of a linked list and an integer k.",
    "output_format": "The rotated linked list.",
    "constraints": [
        "The number of nodes is in the range [0, 500]",
        "-100 <= Node.val <= 100",
        "0 <= k <= 2 * 10^9"
    ],
    "explanation": "To rotate the list by k places, we first find the length n of the list. Since rotating n times results in the same list, we take k = k % n. We then connect the tail of the list to the head to form a circle. Finally, we move n - k steps from the original tail and break the circle there to find the new head.",
    "answer": "class Solution:\n    def rotateRight(self, head: ListNode, k: int) -> ListNode:\n        if not head or not head.next or k == 0: return head\n        n, curr = 1, head\n        while curr.next:\n            curr = curr.next; n += 1\n        curr.next = head; k %= n\n        for _ in range(n - k): curr = curr.next\n        new_head = curr.next; curr.next = None\n        return new_head",
    "boilerplate": {
        "python": "import sys, json\nclass ListNode:\n    def __init__(self, val=0, next=None):\n        self.val = val; self.next = next\ndef rotateRight(head, k):\n    if not head or not head.next or k == 0: return head\n    n, curr = 1, head\n    while curr.next: curr = curr.next; n += 1\n    curr.next = head; k %= n\n    for _ in range(n - k): curr = curr.next\n    new_head = curr.next; curr.next = None\n    return new_head\ndef arr_to_list(arr):\n    if not arr: return None\n    head = ListNode(arr[0]); curr = head\n    for i in range(1, len(arr)): curr.next = ListNode(arr[i]); curr = curr.next\n    return head\ndef list_to_arr(head):\n    res = []; curr = head\n    while curr: res.append(curr.val); curr = curr.next\n    return res\nif __name__ == '__main__':\n    lines = sys.stdin.read().strip().split('\\n')\n    if len(lines) >= 2:\n        arr = json.loads(lines[0]); k = int(lines[1])\n        print(json.dumps(list_to_arr(rotateRight(arr_to_list(arr), k))).replace(' ', ''))",
        "cpp": "#include <iostream>\n#include <vector>\n#include <string>\n#include <sstream>\n#include <algorithm>\nusing namespace std;\nstruct ListNode {\n    int val; ListNode *next;\n    ListNode(int x) : val(x), next(NULL) {}\n};\nListNode* rotateRight(ListNode* head, int k) {\n    if (!head || !head->next || k == 0) return head;\n    int n = 1; ListNode* curr = head;\n    while (curr->next) { curr = curr->next; n++; }\n    curr->next = head; k %= n;\n    int steps = n - k; while (steps--) curr = curr->next;\n    ListNode* newHead = curr->next; curr->next = NULL;\n    return newHead;\n}\nint main() {\n    string line; if (!getline(cin, line)) return 0;\n    int k; if (!(cin >> k)) k = 0;\n    for (char &c : line) if (c == '[' || c == ']' || c == ',') c = ' ';\n    stringstream ss(line); int val; ListNode* head = NULL, *tail = NULL;\n    while (ss >> val) {\n        if (!head) head = tail = new ListNode(val);\n        else { tail->next = new ListNode(val); tail = tail->next; }\n    }\n    ListNode* rotated = rotateRight(head, k);\n    cout << \"[\"; while (rotated) { cout << rotated->val << (rotated->next ? \",\" : \"\"); rotated = rotated->next; } cout << \"]\" << endl;\n    return 0;\n}",
        "java": "import java.util.*;\nimport java.io.*;\nclass ListNode { int val; ListNode next; ListNode(int x) { val = x; } }\npublic class Main {\n    public static ListNode rotateRight(ListNode head, int k) {\n        if (head == null || head.next == null || k == 0) return head;\n        int n = 1; ListNode curr = head;\n        while (curr.next != null) { curr = curr.next; n++; }\n        curr.next = head; k %= n;\n        int steps = n - k; while (steps-- > 0) curr = curr.next;\n        ListNode newHead = curr.next; curr.next = null;\n        return newHead;\n    }\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        String l1 = br.readLine(), l2 = br.readLine();\n        if (l1 == null || l2 == null) return;\n        int k = Integer.parseInt(l2.trim());\n        l1 = l1.replace(\"[\", \"\").replace(\"]\", \"\").replace(\",\", \" \").trim();\n        if (l1.isEmpty()) { System.out.println(\"[]\"); return; }\n        String[] parts = l1.split(\"\\\\s+\");\n        ListNode dummy = new ListNode(0), tail = dummy;\n        for (String p : parts) { tail.next = new ListNode(Integer.parseInt(p)); tail = tail.next; }\n        ListNode rotated = rotateRight(dummy.next, k);\n        System.out.print(\"[\"); while (rotated != null) { System.out.print(rotated.val + (rotated.next != null ? \",\" : \"\")); rotated = rotated.next; } System.out.println(\"]\");\n    }\n}",
        "javascript": "const fs = require('fs');\nfunction ListNode(val, next) { this.val = (val===undefined ? 0 : val); this.next = (next===undefined ? null : next); }\nfunction rotateRight(head, k) {\n    if (!head || !head.next || k === 0) return head;\n    let n = 1, curr = head;\n    while (curr.next) { curr = curr.next; n++; }\n    curr.next = head; k %= n;\n    let steps = n - k; while (steps--) curr = curr.next;\n    const newHead = curr.next; curr.next = null; return newHead;\n}\nconst input = fs.readFileSync(0, 'utf8').trim().split('\\n');\nif (input.length < 2) process.exit(0);\nconst arr = JSON.parse(input[0]); const k = parseInt(input[1]);\nif (arr.length === 0) { console.log(\"[]\"); process.exit(0); }\nlet dummy = new ListNode(0), tail = dummy;\nfor (const v of arr) { tail.next = new ListNode(v); tail = tail.next; }\nlet rotated = rotateRight(dummy.next, k); const res = [];\nwhile (rotated) { res.push(rotated.val); rotated = rotated.next; }\nconsole.log(JSON.stringify(res).replace(/\\s+/g, ''));"
    },
